    "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">ELI302 · Chapter 9 · Session 49</span>\n<h2>Session 49 — Unit 9. QUOTATIONS / ALLUSIONS / TRANSPOSITION</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM syllabus 13743 · session plan</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">ELI302 · Chương 9 · Buổi 49</span>\n<h2>Buổi 49 — Unit 9. QUOTATIONS / ALLUSIONS / TRANSPOSITION</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: syllabus FLM 13743 · kế hoạch buổi</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Type</span><span class=\"v\">Offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">LO9</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">IT</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slides in this lesson</span><span class=\"v\">none from FLM</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Hình thức</span><span class=\"v\">Offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">LO9</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">IT</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slide trong bài</span><span class=\"v\">FLM không có</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>What this session covers (FLM, verbatim)</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nội dung buổi học (FLM, nguyên văn)</h3></div>\n<p>Unit 9. QUOTATIONS / ALLUSIONS / TRANSPOSITION<br>- Review definition of quotation, allusion, and transposition</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Materials to read</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Tài liệu cần đọc</h3></div>\n<p>Coursebook [1], Chapter 12, Cousebook [2], page 177-180, PPT presentation, other teaching resources provided</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Student's tasks</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên</h3></div>\n<p>Read the equivelant units of each lesson before attending class; AI search (ChatGPT or Google Bard) to identify cultural references; verify translation tone via DeepL</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Constructive questions — answer them yourself first</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Câu hỏi kiến tạo — tự trả lời trước</h3></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>HCM_CQ17.1</strong> — How should a lecture be note-taken? You are going to listen to a lecture in English about History. What key points of the lecture will you take note. Demonstrate how you interpret the speech.</li>\n<li><strong>HCM_CQ17.2</strong> — How should a piece of news be note-taken? You are going to listen to some pieces of news. What keys points of the news you are going to take note. Demonstrate how you interpret the peices of news.</li>\n<li><strong>HN_CQ17.1</strong> — How can quotation be recognized in the source speech? How can this be interpreted into Vietnamese?</li>\n<li><strong>HN_CQ17.2</strong> — How can allusion be recognized in the source speech? How can these be interpreted into Vietnamese?</li>\n<li><strong>HN_CQ17.3</strong> — How can transposition be recognized in the source speech? How can these be interpreted into Vietnamese?</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Detailed lecture and 🎬 video for this session: coming later. For now follow the slides, the materials and the tasks above.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Bài giảng chi tiết và 🎬 video cho buổi này: sẽ bổ sung sau. Trước mắt học theo slide, tài liệu và nhiệm vụ ở trên.</div></div>"
